  REBUILT, not pasted. The shape the bare collection returns with
  Accept: application/vnd.sap.adt.transportorganizertree.v1+xml -- the ONLY request that
  answers. Measured 2026-09-09: 270 138 bytes, 6 requests, 14 tasks, 672 objects, in one
  reply with no paging. Reduced here to three requests.

  Four things about this document are the measurement, not the reduction:

    * The wrapper is tm:released and it CARRIES ITS OWN SCOPE: "Released (From Last 2
      Weeks)". There was no tm:modifiable node at all -- the list is released-only and the
      two-week window is written into the data, not into a parameter.
    * tm:request here has TWELVE attributes. No tm:status_text and no tm:source_client:
      the detail resource has those, this one does not.
    * There is no tm:all_objects. The union rule is not optional here, it is the only way
      to know what a request contains.
    * The owners are not all the caller. DEVUSER2 owns DEVK900107 and it appears because
      DEVUSER1 holds a task inside it. That is enumeration of third parties, small and
      declared -- see docs/security.md.
-->
